<title>USA: U.S. April consumer prices rose 0.1 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. April consumer prices rose 0.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Labor Department monthly Consumer Price Index (CPI-U), 1982-84 equals 100:</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:  Seasonally Adj.    Unadjusted</p>
<p>    -			   Apr    Mar     Apr97/96</p>
<p> All Items		    0.1    0.1	2.5</p>
<p> -Excluding Food/Energy   0.3    0.2	2.7</p>
